  Main form for rev_bankaccount — WBS 8.3 (payment capture form). TAD:
  docs/architecture/revitalise-grant-automation-architecture.md section 9.4 (gate consequence 2,
  C-TECH-077 newly applies to this table's 16 secured columns across both finance tables) and
  section 3.1 (rev_bankaccount attribute table). SDD: docs/plans/revitalise-payment-capture-plan.md
  FR-150, FR-154, NFR-150.

  ALL 7 SECURED COLUMNS ON THIS TABLE ARE ON THIS FORM, SATISFYING C-TECH-077 IN THE SAME
  CHANGE THAT CREATES THE FORM (the table's Entity.xml already existed from WBS 8.1 — this is
  the "in the same change" half for a form authored after its columns, which the rule's own
  text anticipates: "or is declared in the gate's own exemption list with a reason" — no
  exemption is needed here because every column gets a control). The 7: rev_accountholdername,
  rev_sortcode, rev_accountnumber, rev_active, rev_applicantid, rev_providerid, rev_payeetype.
  rev_name (unsecured, primary name, ApplicationRequired plain text — NOT autonumber, see this
  table's own Entity.xml header) is also on the form as the account nickname field FR-154
  governs.

  SHAPE COPIED FROM Entities/rev_roundfinance/FormXml/main/{94936d70-...}.xml, per
  skills/how-to-verify-a-platform-contract.md.

  CONTROL CLASSIDS — all ground-truthed against this solution's OWN already-shipped,
  already-imported forms (grep across Entities/*/FormXml, 2026-09-09):
    Text (nvarchar)    {4273EDBD-AC1D-40d3-9FB2-095C621B552D}  — rev_setting.rev_name
    Two Options (bit)  {67FAC785-CD58-4f9f-ABB3-4B7DDC6ED5ED}  — rev_grant.rev_manualacceptancerecorded
    Lookup             {270BD3DB-D9AF-4782-9025-509E298DEC0A}  — rev_application.rev_applicantid
    Picklist (choice)  {3EF39988-22BB-4f0b-BBBE-64B5A3748AEE}  — rev_applicant.rev_agerange

  FR-154 (bank account nickname must not identify a natural person): the control's own field
  Description ("a nickname or masked last-four identifier ... NEVER the full account number")
  is the ONLY intervention available — ADR-046 records that this design claims no mechanical
  enforcement, so no additional control-level attribute is added here beyond the field
  description already carried in Entity.xml.
-->
